  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U4"],
      "pins": ["U4.10", "U4.11", "U4.12"],
      "nets": ["U4.10 (BS0)", "U4.11 (BS1)", "U4.12 (BS2)"],
      "observed": "On the DISPLAY sheet (display.kicad_sch) the three interface‑select pins are strapped as BS0 (pin 10) → VCC, BS1 (pin 11) → GND, BS2 (pin 12) → VCC (the VCC/GND/VCC symbols sit directly above the BS0/BS1/BS2 stubs, with the right‑hand VCC also feeding the R4/R6/R7 pull‑ups). This gives BS[2:0] = 1,0,1.",
      "expected": "The specification states the SSD1306 must be strapped for I2C: 'BS0 (pin 10) → GND; BS1 (pin 11) → VCC; BS2 (pin 12) → GND', i.e. BS[2:0] = 0,1,0, which is the documented I2C mode that makes D0=SCLK and D1/D2=SDA (the DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA nets driven by the MCU).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch: U4 pins 10/11/12 (BS0/BS1/BS2) connected to VCC / GND / VCC respectively"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "BS0 (pin 10) → GND; BS1 (pin 11) → VCC; BS2 (pin 12) → GND ... That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration"}
      ],
      "impact": "With BS[2:0]=101 the SSD1306 is strapped for a parallel/SPI interface, not I2C. The MCU's DISP_SCL (PB13→D0) and DISP_SDA (PB14→D1/D2) lines will not be interpreted as an I2C bus, so the OLED will not respond to the firmware's I2C traffic (display dead / garbled).",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Passive values, pull‑ups, charge‑pump network, NFC bus, touch circuit and SWD header all match the specification; the one deviation is the SSD1306 interface‑select strap, which the drawing ties as BS0=VCC, BS1=GND, BS2=VCC (101) instead of the I2C strap BS0=GND, BS1=VCC, BS2=GND (010) the spec requires, leaving the display unable to communicate over I2C."
}

